# board.pdl - Snake: the grid as DATA for the shared engine game_core (realtime kind, MODE snake). The first ledger row records the hash of this file and rules.pdl:
# editing either after a game began makes every verb refuse that ledger (start a new game).
# MODE  | snake                 the step function: ONE snake on a grid; head, trail, seeded food, wall and self collision, growth (game_core.c snake_step; the plan's M0)
# BOARD | cols|rows | N          the grid (6 to 32 each, at most 1100 cells). The snake starts in the middle heading right, rules.pdl start_len cells long.
# The wall rule (solid or wrap), growth, score and the checkpoint spacing are RULES (rules.pdl), not code.
# The k-th food goes to free[ mix(seed*1000003 + k*16 + 7) % nfree ] (free = unoccupied cells in row-major order when it spawns): the food is a function of the ledger, never stored.
MODE  | snake
BOARD | cols | 16
BOARD | rows | 12
